rota lap 7676, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels. Read foundations/20260826-021732_air-the-row-that-feels.md whole. Air's test is touch: pull on a claimed boundary and see whether it comes free alone. Applied it directly this lap -- the essay's own Bound paragraph names exactly one wire format and one payload shape as what the 3.02x finding rests on, and the scratch probe was built to press on that boundary (run it, read the real bytes) rather than trust hand arithmetic. The claim came free: re-running the probe reproduces the same four numbers, and the finding does not reach further than the one wire format it names.
obs Fourteen fallow readings in a row, each honestly reporting an unchanged state, is itself a finding worth not repeating a fifteenth time -- the lane's own mandate is to generate rather than wait, and no captain's word had landed to end the wait. Breaking the streak cost one essay rather than one more status report.
obs The register and reach fixes this lap needed (48% to 4% negation; grade 16 to 10) are a reminder that a dense, numbers-heavy Field essay drifts past its own ceiling by default and wants a deliberate pass against the scan before it is graded, not after.
